From ab4a2d4e87db3449ef8ea67531451cc826b8f5bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahmed Adel Wafdy <fandes99@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:03:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(autoware_pointcloud_preprocessor): link the filter
 library against CGAL

polygon_remover.cpp and utility/geometry.cpp, built into
pointcloud_preprocessor_filter, use CGAL with GMP numbers, but only
polygon_remover_node links gmp and CGAL. The library has undefined GMP
symbols, which lazy binding hides until they are called. Linked with
-z now, dlopen fails ("undefined symbol: __gmpz_set_si") and no
component in the library loads: crop box, distortion corrector, ring
outlier, concatenate and downsample filters.

Link it the same way as polygon_remover_node.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Ahmed Adel Wafdy <fandes99@gmail.com>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index a5b2652fa4..e8fdac7aed 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -144,6 +144,9 @@ target_link_libraries(pointcloud_preprocessor_filter
   ${Sophus_LIBRARIES}
   ${PCL_LIBRARIES}
   ${tf2_sensor_msgs_LIBRARIES}
+  gmp
+  CGAL::CGAL
+  CGAL::CGAL_Core
 )
 
 target_include_directories(pointcloud_preprocessor_filter PRIVATE
-- 
